# 基础词 Unit04
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit04核心词汇

{{appeal}}{/əˈpiːl/}{{v. 呼吁；吸引；n. 上诉}}{{The charity appealed to the public for donations.}}
{{appear}}{/əˈpɪər/}{{v. 出现；似乎}}{{The sun appeared from behind the clouds.}}
{{appetite}}{/ˈæpɪtaɪt/}{{n. 食欲；胃口}}{{The long walk gave me a good appetite.}}
{{apple}}{/ˈæpl/}{{n. 苹果}}{{An apple a day keeps the doctor away.}}
{{apply}}{/əˈplaɪ/}{{v. 申请；应用；适用}}{{She applied for a scholarship to study abroad.}}
{{appoint}}{/əˈpɔɪnt/}{{v. 任命；指定}}{{He was appointed as the new manager.}}
{{appreciate}}{/əˈpriːʃieɪt/}{{v. 欣赏；感激}}{{I really appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{approach}}{/əˈprəʊtʃ/}{{v. 接近；n. 方法；途径}}{{We need a new approach to solve this problem.}}
{{appropriate}}{/əˈprəʊpriət/}{{adj. 适当的；恰当的}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the occasion.}}
{{approve}}{/əˈpruːv/}{{v. 批准；赞成}}{{The board approved the new budget plan.}}
{{approximate}}{/əˈprɒksɪmət/}{{adj. 大约的；近似的}}{{The approximate cost of the project is one million dollars.}}
{{architect}}{/ˈɑːrkɪtekt/}{{n. 建筑师；设计师}}{{The architect designed a beautiful modern building.}}
{{area}}{/ˈeəriə/}{{n. 地区；领域；面积}}{{This area is known for its beautiful scenery.}}
{{argue}}{/ˈɑːrɡjuː/}{{v. 争论；辩论}}{{They argued about the best way to solve the problem.}}
{{arise}}{/əˈraɪz/}{{v. 出现；产生}}{{Unexpected problems may arise during the process.}}
{{arm}}{/ɑːrm/}{{n. 手臂；武器；v. 武装}}{{The country armed itself for potential conflict.}}
{{army}}{/ˈɑːrmi/}{{n. 军队；陆军}}{{He served in the army for ten years.}}
{{around}}{/əˈraʊnd/}{{prep. 围绕；adv. 到处}}{{There are trees around the house.}}
{{arrange}}{/əˈreɪndʒ/}{{v. 安排；整理}}{{She arranged the flowers in a beautiful vase.}}
{{arrest}}{/əˈrest/}{{v./n. 逮捕}}{{The police arrested the suspect last night.}}
{{arrival}}{/əˈraɪvl/}{{n. 到达；到来}}{{The arrival of the train was delayed by one hour.}}
{{arrive}}{/əˈraɪv/}{{v. 到达}}{{We arrived at the airport just in time.}}
{{arrow}}{/ˈærəʊ/}{{n. 箭；箭头}}{{The arrow hit the target in the center.}}
{{art}}{/ɑːrt/}{{n. 艺术；技术}}{{She has a deep appreciation for modern art.}}
{{article}}{/ˈɑːrtɪkl/}{{n. 文章；物品；冠词}}{{She wrote an interesting article for the newspaper.}}
{{artificial}}{/ˌɑːrtɪˈfɪʃl/}{{adj. 人工的；人造的}}{{Artificial intelligence is changing many industries.}}
{{aside}}{/əˈsaɪd/}{{adv. 在旁边；到旁边}}{{She stepped aside to let others pass.}}
{{ask}}{/ɑːsk/}{{v. 问；请求}}{{May I ask you a question about the assignment?}}
{{aspect}}{/ˈæspekt/}{{n. 方面；角度}}{{We need to consider every aspect of the problem.}}
{{assess}}{/əˈses/}{{v. 评估；评定}}{{The teacher assessed the students' performance.}}
{{asset}}{/ˈæset/}{{n. 资产；有价值的人或物}}{{Her experience is a great asset to the company.}}
{{assign}}{/əˈsaɪn/}{{v. 分配；指派}}{{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{assist}}{/əˈsɪst/}{{v. 帮助；协助}}{{The nurse assisted the doctor during the surgery.}}
{{associate}}{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt/}{{v. 联系；n. 合伙人}}{{People often associate the color red with passion.}}
{{assume}}{/əˈsjuːm/}{{v. 假定；承担}}{{We cannot assume that everyone agrees with us.}}
{{assure}}{/əˈʃʊər/}{{v. 保证；使确信}}{{I assure you that everything will be fine.}}
{{atmosphere}}{/ˈætməsfɪər/}{{n. 大气；气氛}}{{The restaurant has a warm and friendly atmosphere.}}
{{attach}}{/əˈtætʃ/}{{v. 附上；系；使依恋}}{{Please attach your photo to the application form.}}
{{attack}}{/əˈtæk/}{{v./n. 攻击；发作}}{{The army launched a surprise attack at dawn.}}
{{attain}}{/əˈteɪn/}{{v. 达到；获得}}{{She attained the highest score in the exam.}}
